rules_version = '2';

// CSA65 Quiz Management System — Firebase Storage Security Rules
//
// NEW IN THIS CHANGE. The storage bucket has been named in
// js/firebase-config.js since the project was created but was never written
// to; lib/materialStore.js is its first use, so these rules are its first
// protection. Deploy them BEFORE the first upload:
//   firebase deploy --only storage
// or paste into Firebase console → Storage → Rules. Keep this file as the
// source of truth, the same way firestore.rules is.
//
// DENY EVERYTHING. There is no client path to this bucket at all — not for
// students, not for signed-in teachers.
//
// Why even teachers are denied here: every legitimate access already goes
// through a serverless function holding a verified teacher token
// (api/upload-material.js, api/process-material.js), and those use the Admin
// SDK, which bypasses these rules entirely. Allowing a parallel client-side
// route would widen the attack surface to protect a path nothing uses.
// Teacher downloads are served as short-lived signed URLs minted server-side
// by MaterialStore.getDownloadUrl() — also unaffected by these rules.
//
// This answers §10's "can students download assessment material?" with a
// structural no, rather than with obscurity: uploaded material is the source
// the answer key is derived from, so it inherits the keyword bank's trust
// level (server-only), not the question bank's (deliberately public — see the
// asymmetry note in firestore.rules).
service firebase.storage {
  match /b/{bucket}/o {
    match /{allPaths=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
